  "rules": {
    "summary": "10 teams, 33 games each (NBL27: 165 games, 19 September 2026 to 14 February 2027). The ladder ranks by win percentage, then points percentage (points for over points against). The top six play the Finals: 1st and 2nd go straight to the semi-finals; 3rd hosts 4th (the winner meets 2nd), 5th hosts 6th, and the 3 v 4 loser hosts the 5 v 6 winner (that winner meets 1st). Semi-finals are best of three and the Championship Series best of five, the higher ladder place hosting games 1, 3 and 5. Ignite Cup games count on the ladder; the Ignite Cup Finals do not. NBL27's finals have not been announced separately; this is the NBL26 format, used since the play-in arrived in NBL23.",
